Langerhanes cell (LC) histiocytes are rare in scaffold-matured individuals and generally occur at a younger age. Most cases of skeletal LCH arise from the involvement of bone, skin, respiratory and gastrointestinal sites. It is rare for people to have a head and neck involved. So far, no cases of LCH in the skeletal system have been published.
